WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.814 --> 00:00:05.666
♪ Me and Gary Vee up in the office ♪

00:00:05.666 --> 00:00:07.670
- [Man] What's cooking?

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:08.860
- It's my last week at VaynerMedia.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.150
- [Man] I'm aware.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.453
- It's crazy, I know, I've
been here three years.

00:00:12.453 --> 00:00:13.740
- What are you doing?

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.690
- So, I'm going through
a very big life change

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:18.700
and I am leaving advertising,

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.530
leaving New York City,
leaving the country.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:22.475
I'm just going to go
travel for like a year.

00:00:22.475 --> 00:00:23.825
- Good for you.

00:00:23.825 --> 00:00:26.300
- I wanted to do it for a
really really long time and--

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.900
- The sooner the better
with shit like that.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.380
- I know, and I want to go into like

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.150
the health and wellness, medicine world.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.650
- You look good.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:36.930
- Thanks.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.410
Yeah, I've been uh,

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.130
I definitely feel better than I used to.

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:40.963
That's for sure.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:45.930
So, yeah, it's a big career
change you can't make overnight.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:46.870
So, I was like, well, I might as well

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:49.772
take advantage of the
time and really like,

00:00:49.772 --> 00:00:51.700
get some clarity and think about things

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.680
a little bit, because you can't make

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.605
big decisions like that when
you're so in the thick of it.

00:00:54.605 --> 00:00:55.438
- In it.

00:00:55.438 --> 00:00:56.470
- You're like, "I have no perspective,

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.170
I can't see anything".

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.030
- So right.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:01.550
- So yeah, I mean, I feel like there was

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.342
so many factors that kind
of played a role and--

00:01:04.342 --> 00:01:05.489
- Of course.

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:07.960
- But I don't know, the
past couple of months like,

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.700
all the cards kind of lined up perfectly

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:10.864
and I was just like, "This is right."

00:01:10.864 --> 00:01:11.890
- Good for you.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:13.550
- So, yeah.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:14.880
- Thank you for everything.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.170
- Thank you, I mean it's
been an awesome three years.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:19.620
Like, I mean I told Shirley this

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:20.737
and I'll tell Claud this later,

00:01:20.737 --> 00:01:24.240
at the end of the day I really do.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.220
I leave with a lot of good vibes

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:29.840
and I felt very, just
like loved and supported,

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.010
and you don't find that
at a lot of agencies,

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.080
or a lot of places in general.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:38.160
Yeah, it's been a great experience,

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.180
I'm super grateful for
it, it's weird to leave.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:44.097
- Is there anything I can help
with in this next chapter?

00:01:44.097 --> 00:01:46.510
- Probably, at some point for sure.

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:47.810
- Yeah, don't be shy.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:49.510
- No, I won't, trust me, I won't.

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:50.343
- I believe you.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.430
- I'll definitely like--

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:53.079
- I know what makes you good.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.590
- If I can think about anything,

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:56.655
I think I need to kind of figure out--

00:01:56.655 --> 00:01:57.488
- What?

00:01:57.488 --> 00:01:59.040
- That world I want to go into is so huge

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.140
and it's getting really cluttered,

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:02.653
and it's getting really,
just like inauthentic.

00:02:02.653 --> 00:02:05.280
- Can I give you a quick piece of advice?

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.113
- Please.

00:02:06.113 --> 00:02:07.180
- Every world is like that.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:08.013
- Yeah.

00:02:08.013 --> 00:02:08.846
- Don't let that cripple you.

00:02:08.846 --> 00:02:09.679
- Yeah.

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:11.474
- And go narrow to what makes you pop.

00:02:11.474 --> 00:02:12.307
- Right.

00:02:12.307 --> 00:02:15.904
- Motivational speakers are
my most hated people, yet--

00:02:15.904 --> 00:02:16.737
- You mean by other people?

00:02:16.737 --> 00:02:17.576
- I hate them.

00:02:17.576 --> 00:02:18.409
- Oh.

00:02:18.409 --> 00:02:20.310
- Yet I get categorized in
that world all the time.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:21.143
- Right.

00:02:21.143 --> 00:02:22.370
- But I'm not crippled because I know

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.049
that I'm not trying to do the wrong thing.

00:02:24.049 --> 00:02:26.880
- Right, or you're not
trying to do whatever.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.783
- The wrong thing.

00:02:27.783 --> 00:02:28.616
- Yeah.

00:02:28.616 --> 00:02:29.570
- This is, forget about that.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:30.403
- Yeah.

00:02:30.403 --> 00:02:32.577
- If you don't ever look
for the white space.

00:02:32.577 --> 00:02:34.030
It doesn't exist.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:36.110
- Hm, yeah, just like make it be your own.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.856
- Do what the fuck you know.

00:02:37.856 --> 00:02:39.006
- What you're good at.

00:02:39.006 --> 00:02:39.839
- Like if you know yoga.

00:02:39.839 --> 00:02:40.672
- Right.

00:02:40.672 --> 00:02:42.060
- Yoga's plenty fucking
(mumbles), you know.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:42.893
- Yeah.

00:02:42.893 --> 00:02:45.194
- Be in the cream rises
to the top business.

00:02:45.194 --> 00:02:46.477
- Yeah.

00:02:46.477 --> 00:02:47.320
- Not in the I'm going to see

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:48.840
something no one else sees business.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.080
- Right, and that's not the way.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.210
I don't want to look at this as like

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.113
a business opportunity, of like,

00:02:52.113 --> 00:02:53.670
let me go travel the world and

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.150
find these trendy things and bring them.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:56.780
Like that's not what I, I truly want

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.150
to find a way to like, help people who are

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:00.860
chronically ill, and cannot feed...

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.212
They don't have the resources,
or something like that.

00:03:02.212 --> 00:03:03.693
I'm not sure exactly what it is but--

00:03:03.693 --> 00:03:05.050
- So, all the people that are doing

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.000
the wrong thing, crowded, not authentic,

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.540
it just has nothing to do with you.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.400
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.676
- I'm not crippled by other agencies

00:03:12.676 --> 00:03:15.210
sucking up, giving a fuck about people.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.981
- Yeah and if you were, you wouldn't

00:03:16.981 --> 00:03:19.750
be where you are, because you can't--

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:20.920
- That's the thing you need to do.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.710
- Yeah, that's a good piece of advice.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.589
- It's a really good
piece of advice, like--

00:03:25.589 --> 00:03:27.115
- Yeah.

00:03:27.115 --> 00:03:29.080
- What do you want to do?

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:30.600
And do it.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.020
And literally eliminate every other--

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:32.853
- That's actually really simple

00:03:32.853 --> 00:03:33.686
when you think about it, like--

00:03:33.686 --> 00:03:35.060
- It's super fucking simple.

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:37.060
- We get so in our heads--

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:39.380
- 'Cause we get taught, we get taught.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:40.213
- Yeah.

00:03:40.213 --> 00:03:41.711
- We get taught, and I think in hindsight,

00:03:41.711 --> 00:03:43.843
my inability to learn that way--

00:03:43.843 --> 00:03:44.770
- Mhm.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:46.040
- Became my greatest strength.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:48.380
- Yeah, and I feel like, but once you

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.250
learn that way, it's very
hard to unlearn that.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.446
- It's very hard, the same way
I can't do the other thing,

00:03:52.446 --> 00:03:55.168
I can't learn anything the normal way.

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:56.001
- Yeah.

00:03:56.001 --> 00:03:56.834
- You know?

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:58.460
- Yeah, well a lot of people are like

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.535
"You know, what you're
doing it's kind of risky,"

00:04:00.535 --> 00:04:02.480
and I'm like, I don't know--

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:03.313
- Risky for what?

00:04:03.313 --> 00:04:04.860
- I just don't believe
in this whole notion

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.735
of like, okay you graduate, and you work

00:04:06.735 --> 00:04:07.568
then get married, have kids and--

00:04:07.568 --> 00:04:09.038
- You can pick up back from, come back

00:04:09.038 --> 00:04:10.740
and work here, you're in the same spot.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.037
- Yeah, I also just don't think--

00:04:12.037 --> 00:04:14.022
- I actually think it's,
the other way is risky.

00:04:14.022 --> 00:04:16.011
- Me too, because I think it's really

00:04:16.011 --> 00:04:18.690
easy to become complacent, and--

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:19.523
- 100%!

00:04:19.523 --> 00:04:21.838
- I don't know, I don't think it's

00:04:21.838 --> 00:04:23.950
deviating from a path because I don't

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.260
think that there is a path.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:26.712
- There's way too much respect for

00:04:26.712 --> 00:04:28.926
anybody who thinks what
you're doing is risky.

00:04:28.926 --> 00:04:30.970
- Yeah, I mean I've literally gotten

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:31.990
that response from like one person

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:34.273
but my family is like, "Yes, 100%, go"

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:35.160
- That's awesome.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.650
- And they're so supportive.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:38.650
- And the person that's,
you know, saying that,

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:41.250
is you know, respects a certain narrative

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:42.252
and that's awesome too.

00:04:42.252 --> 00:04:43.730
- Right, and that's great for them.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:44.824
- And may be great for them forever.

00:04:44.824 --> 00:04:45.880
- Right.
- May be.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:47.793
- Right, but yeah I've always been

00:04:47.793 --> 00:04:49.447
pushed and questioned a little bit,

00:04:49.447 --> 00:04:50.280
- Yeah.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:51.113
- So I knew that this was going to happen

00:04:51.113 --> 00:04:52.938
at some point, it was
just a matter of when.

00:04:52.938 --> 00:04:55.248
- Well, I'm happy to help when
you get through the process.

00:04:55.248 --> 00:04:57.864
- Thank you, yeah, I will definitely

00:04:57.864 --> 00:04:59.870
hit you up on that at some point,

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:01.924
when I have kind of like, some clarity

00:05:01.924 --> 00:05:04.220
about life, and when I'm back.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.710
If I come back, who knows.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:07.286
- Okay. Where you going?

00:05:07.286 --> 00:05:09.250
- Well I was going to do South America,

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:10.980
but I just changed to now I'm going

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:13.010
to do Asia, because I want to spend

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:15.410
some time in India and do, like Chinese,

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:19.461
like ancient, Ayurvedic
medicine and study that,

00:05:19.461 --> 00:05:21.460
and probably spend some time in

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:23.445
Indonesia too, and Napal, like farming.

00:05:23.445 --> 00:05:24.930
- That's cool.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.330
- It just is a place that aligns more

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:27.470
with like, my personal interests

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.155
than other parts of the world, so...

00:05:29.155 --> 00:05:30.210
- I love it.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:33.184
- Yeah, so I'll leave
for Vietnam in March.

00:05:33.184 --> 00:05:34.060
- Amazing.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:34.893
- Which is fine because--

00:05:34.893 --> 00:05:35.726
- What are you going to do in February?

00:05:35.726 --> 00:05:36.559
Just kinda--

00:05:36.559 --> 00:05:37.830
- I'm going home, to Oklahoma

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:38.663
to just like, be with my parents.

00:05:38.663 --> 00:05:39.590
- That's amazing.

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:41.072
- I don't ever see them
so, thank you so much.

00:05:41.072 --> 00:05:42.443
- Thank you for everything, really.

00:05:42.443 --> 00:05:43.790
- No really, you too.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.130
- I mean it, ping me if you need me.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.713
(smooth music)

